senses.gloss:
khaṭu
(1) = khaṭa: Divy 〔173.10〕 khaṭu-capeṭādibhis;
(2) khaṭv-ākārān (sattvān) Divy 〔338.8〕 (here Dutt, MSV 〔iv.38.17 note〕, cites Tib. as gtun, pestle); 〔342.11〕 (here Dutt, ib. 〔44.19〕, cites Tib. as phar [read phor] pa, said to mean saraka, a drinking vessel); but 〔342.26, 343.5〕 replaces this by what is meant for taṭṭv-āk˚, see s.v. taṭṭu; so read each time.
